.\" ABSD manual page source (mdoc(7)); rendered by scripts/render-man.sh.
.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt OD 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm od
.Nd dump files in octal, hexadecimal and other formats (sbase)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl bdosvx
.Op Fl A Ar addressformat
.Op Fl E | Fl e
.Op Fl j Ar skip
.Op Fl t Ar outputformat
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is sbase 0.1's
.Nm od ,
built unpatched for ABSD with the C kit; see
.Xr sbase 7 .
It writes the bytes of the named files, or of standard input, as octal,
decimal, hexadecimal or character values, with
.Fl t
.Pq for example Ql -t x1 No or Ql -t c
choosing the format and
.Fl A
the address base.
For the conventional hexadecimal display modes, see
.Xr hexdump 1 .
.Sh UNSUPPORTED ON ABSD
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c
not in sbase 0.1: usage error, status 1;
.Fl t Cm c
works.
.It messages
prefixed with
.Ql argv[0]
as invoked;
.Ql strerror
texts are Picolibc's.
.El
.Pp
Behaviour on ABSD is predicted until the guest qualification
.Pq Xr sbase 7 .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on an error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
absd$ od -A x -t x1 /home/operator/prog | head -n 4
absd$ printf 'a\etb\en' | od -t c
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cmp 1 ,
.Xr sbase 7
